      "week": 4,
      "day": 22,
      "title": "Hontanas -> Itero de la Vega",
  "distance": "20,7 km",
  "time": "5 hours 31 min",
  "short_desc": "Meseta day 3. Friends from All a round the World, a steep climb, and pilgrim inner with Paula",
  "long_desc": " We stayed at the charming Villa Fontanas in the small village of Hontanas, a pleasant surprise along the Camino. Last night, we enjoyed a wonderful dinner with our Camino friends: Daniel from San Diego, a Lexie from Melbourne, a man from Flensburg in Germany, Max from Bristol, and a woman from Ireland. Laughter, stories, and true Camino spirit filled the evening. Today’s walk took us through Castrojeriz, a picturesque village we had actually visited back in 2022 during a “try-out” pilgrimage trip with Rolfs Resor. After leaving town, we faced a fairly steep one-kilometer climb, short, but intense! We had to hurry to reach Itero de la Vega by 3:00 p.m. sharp, as we had made a reservation and didn’t want to risk losing it. We made it with five minutes to spare, a small but satisfying victory. Even with a booking, punctuality is key during this busy season on the Camino. Have to do it the Spanish way. In the evening, we were treated to a delicious pilgrim dinner, lovingly prepared by our host Paula. We dined with Laura & Adam, who run a YouTube channel about the Camino, along with fellow pilgrims from Denmark, Germany, the UK, and Australia. Great food, great company and yet another day that reminds us why we’re walking. It’s the people and pilgrims you meet along the way that truly make the Camino unforgettabl!",
